From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] phy: allwinner: add the A733 COMB1 combo-PHY in its PCIe personality

The A733 has two combo PHYs. COMB0 carries USB3-SS and DisplayPort and is
driven by `phy-allwinner-a733-add-serdes-combophy`. COMB1 carries either USB3-SS or PCIe, one lane, and on this
board the protocol mux selects PCIe. This is the PCIe half of COMB1, and
without it there is no link for a controller to train.

A SEPARATE DRIVER, AND WHY

`phy-allwinner-a733-add-serdes-combophy` is 2800 lines of Type-C orientation handling, DisplayPort rate
negotiation and AUX/HPD, none of which exists on COMB1 -- and it drives
hardware that works today. Threading a fourth mode through its init and reset
paths buys a regression risk on a running subsystem for about forty lines of
shared code (a 16-bit write helper and the shape of a table). `phy-allwinner-a733-add-serdes-combophy`'s own header
says DP-alt and PCIe are out of its scope; this keeps that promise instead of
quietly breaking it.

WHERE THE VALUES COME FROM

The wrapper registers are documented: A733 UM V1.00, SERDES chapter, gives
LINK_CTRL0/1, LANE0_CTRL0 and LINK_STUS0 with their fields, and the protocol
mux at 0x6C44 with 001 = PCIe0 lane 0.

The PMA body at 0x06CA0000 is not in the UM at all. Its 84 words were extracted
mechanically from the vendor driver -- not transcribed -- and then classified
against the table `phy-allwinner-a733-add-serdes-combophy` already carries for COMB0:

  49  same index AND same value as the COMB0 table
  17  same index, different value
  18  index not in the COMB0 table

Each line in the table says which class it is in. The 49 are as understood as
COMB0 is, and the same word carrying the same value on a different PHY instance
in a different protocol is itself evidence that those offsets are
protocol-independent. The other 35 are magic values and are marked as such
rather than presented as derived; deriving them is open work, as are the two LINK_CTRL1
fields where the vendor value uses encodings the UM calls reserved, and an
addressing ambiguity in three of the accesses.

WHAT THIS COVERS THAT THE VENDOR DOES NOT

 - PMA_CMN_READY is polled with a timeout. The vendor spins in while(true) with
   a 100 us delay and no way out: a PHY that never reports ready hangs the boot
   instead of failing the probe.
 - The PCIe controller's bus gates are NOT touched here. The vendor sets them
   from its PHY path; they gate the controller's own AXI and AHB access, so they
   belong to the controller's node, which claims them as clocks.
 - The reference-clock gate is claimed as a clock, not poked in a register
   window this driver does not own.
 - The vendor's last fixup reads a word, computes a value from it and then
   overwrites both with a constant. Only the constant survives here, with a note,
   so nobody maintains arithmetic that never had an effect.

ONE SHARP EDGE, AND IT IS IN THE MAPPING

The middle register window (0x06C06000) holds the protocol mux of BOTH combo
PHYs, and `phy-allwinner-a733-add-serdes-combophy` claims it as an exclusive region. So this driver maps it with
devm_ioremap() instead of requesting it: requesting it twice fails with -EBUSY
and would take PCIe down whenever USB3 probed first -- an ordering nobody
controls. The AUX/HPD PHY solves the same overlap the same way.

Verified: compile-check builds the object clean. No hardware effect on its own
-- a PHY with no consumer is never initialised; the proof belongs to the patch
that adds the controller node.

Based on drivers/phy/sunxi-cadence-combophy.c from radxa/allwinner-bsp
(commit b36af3872d4e, "aiot-linux-v1.4.6 release"; the file is unchanged on
the branches cubie-aiot-v1.4.6 and cubie-aiot-v1.4.8), GPL-2.0,
Copyright(c) 2020 - 2023 Allwinner Technology Co.,Ltd. and
Copyright (C) 2024 Allwinner Electronics Co., Ltd. The 84 PMA words come
from its sunxi_cadence_phy_pcie_phy_init():
https://github.com/radxa/allwinner-bsp/blob/b36af3872d4e6e91da6e929f4ccf4822b3ea9d66/drivers/phy/sunxi-cadence-combophy.c

Assisted-by: Claude

diff --git a/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun60i-a733-pcie-combophy.c b/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun60i-a733-pcie-combophy.c
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun60i-a733-pcie-combophy.c
@@ -0,0 +1,430 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
+/*
+ * Allwinner A733 (sun60iw2) COMB1 combo-PHY, PCIe personality.
+ *
+ * The A733 has two combo PHYs in its SERDES subsystem. COMB0 carries USB3-SS
+ * and DisplayPort and is driven by phy-sun60i-a733-combophy.c. COMB1 carries
+ * either USB3-SS or PCIe, one lane, and on this board the protocol mux selects
+ * PCIe (SUBSYS_COMB1_PIPE at 0x06C06C44 reads 0x1 whenever something drives
+ * it). This driver is the PCIe half of COMB1.
+ *
+ * It is a separate driver rather than a third personality inside the COMB0 one
+ * for two reasons that are about risk, not taste: that driver is 2800 lines of
+ * Type-C orientation handling, DisplayPort rate negotiation and AUX/HPD, none
+ * of which exists on COMB1 -- and it runs working hardware today, so threading
+ * a fourth mode through its init and reset paths buys a regression risk for no
+ * shared code. What the two do share is the shape of a PMA table and a 16-bit
+ * write helper, about forty lines.
+ *
+ * WHAT THE REGISTERS ARE
+ *
+ * Three windows, all named by the UM (A733 UM V1.00, SERDES subsystem):
+ *
+ *   link  0x06C02000  COMB1_PHY_PINS_* -- the wrapper. Documented: LINK_CTRL0
+ *                     at 0x0000 (bit0 PHY reset), LINK_CTRL1 at 0x0004
+ *                     (bit28 EN_REFCLK, bit24/20 PLL refclk select, bit16
+ *                     termination, [13:12] refclk divider, [5:4] refclk mode),
+ *                     LANE0_CTRL0 at 0x0100 ([5:4] lane mode, bit0 lane reset),
+ *                     LINK_STUS0 at 0x0900 (bit0 PMA_CMN_READY).
+ *   top2  0x06C06000  the protocol mux at +0xC44: [3:0] 000 = USB3.1,
+ *                     001 = PCIe0 lane 0. Reset value is 0xF.
+ *   pma   0x06CA0000  the PMA/PCS body. NOT in the UM, at all. 128 KiB of
+ *                     16-bit words addressed by index.
+ *
+ * WHERE THE PMA VALUES COME FROM, AND WHAT IS STILL UNKNOWN
+ *
+ * The vendor BSP programs 84 words here (sunxi-cadence-combophy.c, Copyright(c) 2020 - 2023
+ * Allwinner Technology Co.,Ltd., (C) 2024 Allwinner Electronics Co., Ltd.). They were extracted
+ * mechanically from it, not transcribed, and classified against our COMB0 driver's table:
+ *
+ *   49  same index AND same value as the COMB0 USB3 table (`phy-allwinner-a733-add-serdes-combophy`)
+ *   17  same index, different value -- offset meaning transfers, value does not
+ *   18  index not in the COMB0 table at all
+ *
+ * The 49 are as understood as COMB0 is: the same word, the same value, on a
+ * different PHY instance in a different protocol -- which is itself evidence
+ * that those offsets carry protocol-independent common/bias configuration. The
+ * other 35 are magic values. They are marked as such per line below, not presented
+ * as derived, and deriving them is open work. Nothing in the UM covers this
+ * window, so no amount of reading closes that gap; it needs measurement.
+ *
+ * WHAT THIS DOES THAT THE VENDOR DRIVER DOES NOT
+ *
+ *  - PMA_CMN_READY is polled with a timeout. The vendor spins in while(true)
+ *    with a 100 us delay and no way out; a PHY that never reports ready hangs
+ *    the boot instead of failing the probe.
+ *  - The bus gates of the PCIe controller (SUBSYS_PCIE_BGR bits 18/17/16) are
+ *    NOT touched here. The vendor sets them from its PHY path; they gate the
+ *    controller's own AXI and AHB access, so they belong to the controller's
+ *    node, which claims them as clocks.
+ *  - The reference-clock gate (SUBSYS_DBG_CTRL bit29) is a clock and is claimed
+ *    as one, instead of being poked in a register window this driver does not
+ *    own.
+ *  - The vendor's fixup at the end reads a word, computes a value from it and
+ *    then discards both by assigning a constant. Only the constant is kept here,
+ *    with that noted, so nobody maintains arithmetic that never had an effect.
+ *
+ * Copyright (C) 2026 DockSeed
+ */
+
+#include <linux/clk.h>
+#include <linux/delay.h>
+#include <linux/io.h>
+#include <linux/iopoll.h>
+#include <linux/module.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>
+#include <linux/phy/phy.h>
+#include <linux/platform_device.h>
+#include <linux/reset.h>
+
+/* link window (0x06C02000) */
+#define A733_PCIE_LINK_CTRL0		0x0000
+#define  A733_PCIE_LINK_RESET_N		BIT(0)
+#define A733_PCIE_LINK_CTRL1		0x0004
+#define  A733_PCIE_LINK_EN_REFCLK	BIT(28)
+#define A733_PCIE_LANE0_CTRL0		0x0100
+#define  A733_PCIE_LANE0_MODE		GENMASK(5, 4)
+#define  A733_PCIE_LANE0_RESET_N_SW	BIT(0)
+#define A733_PCIE_LINK_STUS0		0x0900
+#define  A733_PCIE_PMA_CMN_READY	BIT(0)
+
+/* top2 window (0x06C06000) */
+#define A733_PCIE_PIPE_TXD_MAP		0x0C44
+#define  A733_PCIE_PIPE_TXD_MAP_PCIE0	0x1
+
+/*
+ * LINK_CTRL1 as the vendor writes it before touching the PMA: refclk taken
+ * from the internal path (bit24 PLL1 select, bit0 digital select), termination
+ * off, divider and mode left at 0. ⚠ The UM marks the internal-mode encoding
+ * 00 in [9:8] as reserved and recommends [13:12] = 10 for a 100 MHz reference,
+ * and this value uses neither -- it is what runs on this board, and nothing here settles
+ * the question.
+ */
+#define A733_PCIE_LINK_CTRL1_INIT	0x01100001
+
+/* PMA words are 16 bit, addressed by index */
+struct a733_pcie_pma_write {
+	u16 idx;
+	u16 val;
+};
+
+struct a733_pcie_combophy {
+	struct device		*dev;
+	void __iomem		*link;
+	void __iomem		*top2;
+	void __iomem		*pma;
+	struct clk		*serdes_clk;
+	struct clk		*refclk;
+	struct reset_control	*reset;
+	struct phy		*phy;
+};
+
+static void a733_pcie_pma_write(struct a733_pcie_combophy *cp, u16 idx, u16 val)
+{
+	writew(val, cp->pma + ((u32)idx << 1));
+}
+
+static void a733_pcie_pma_write_all(struct a733_pcie_combophy *cp,
+				    const struct a733_pcie_pma_write *tbl,
+				    size_t n)
+{
+	size_t i;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < n; i++)
+		a733_pcie_pma_write(cp, tbl[i].idx, tbl[i].val);
+}
+
+static void a733_pcie_rmw(void __iomem *reg, u32 clr, u32 set)
+{
+	u32 val = readl(reg);
+
+	val &= ~clr;
+	val |= set;
+	writel(val, reg);
+}
+
+/* PMA, first block: 25 writes before the lane is put into PCIe mode */
+static const struct a733_pcie_pma_write a733_pcie_pma_pre[] = {
+	{ 0x0022, 0x001A },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x002A, 0x0034 },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x002C, 0x00DA },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x0032, 0x0034 },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x0034, 0x00DA },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x0064, 0x0082 },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x0065, 0x0082 },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x0074, 0x001A },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x0104, 0x0020 },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x0105, 0x0007 },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x010C, 0x0020 },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x010D, 0x0007 },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x0114, 0x030C },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x0115, 0x0007 },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x0124, 0x0007 },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x0125, 0x0003 },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x0126, 0x000F },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x0128, 0x0132 },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x40C0, 0x0208 },	/* PCIe only */
+	{ 0x40C2, 0x009C },	/* PCIe only */
+	{ 0x8044, 0x001A },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x8045, 0x0082 },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x804C, 0x001A },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x804D, 0x0082 },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x4123, 0x0A28 },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+};
+
+/* PMA, second block: PLL, equalisation and lane tuning */
+static const struct a733_pcie_pma_write a733_pcie_pma_post[] = {
+	{ 0x0094, 0x0004 },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x00A4, 0x0004 },	/* PCIe only */
+	{ 0x00D4, 0x0004 },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x01A4, 0x0509 },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x01B4, 0x0509 },	/* PCIe only */
+	{ 0x01C4, 0x0509 },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x01A5, 0x0F00 },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x01B5, 0x0F00 },	/* PCIe only */
+	{ 0x01C5, 0x0F00 },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x01A6, 0x0F08 },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x01B6, 0x0F08 },	/* PCIe only */
+	{ 0x01C6, 0x0F08 },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x0090, 0x0180 },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x00A0, 0x0133 },	/* PCIe only */
+	{ 0x00D0, 0x0133 },	/* COMB0 offset, PCIe value */
+	{ 0x0091, 0x9D8A },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x00A1, 0xB13B },	/* PCIe only */
+	{ 0x00D1, 0xB13B },	/* COMB0 offset, PCIe value */
+	{ 0x0092, 0x0002 },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x00A2, 0x0002 },	/* PCIe only */
+	{ 0x00D2, 0x0002 },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x0093, 0x0102 },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x00A3, 0x00CE },	/* PCIe only */
+	{ 0x00D3, 0x00CE },	/* COMB0 offset, PCIe value */
+	{ 0x01A0, 0x0022 },	/* COMB0 offset, PCIe value */
+	{ 0x01B0, 0x0022 },	/* PCIe only */
+	{ 0x01C0, 0x0022 },	/* COMB0 offset, PCIe value */
+	{ 0x0098, 0x0001 },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x00A8, 0x0001 },	/* PCIe only */
+	{ 0x00D8, 0x0001 },	/* COMB0 offset, PCIe value */
+	{ 0x0099, 0x045F },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x00A9, 0x02F0 },	/* PCIe only */
+	{ 0x00D9, 0x0399 },	/* COMB0 offset, PCIe value */
+	{ 0x009A, 0x006B },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x00AA, 0x0068 },	/* PCIe only */
+	{ 0x00DA, 0x0068 },	/* COMB0 offset, PCIe value */
+	{ 0x009B, 0x0004 },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x00AB, 0x0004 },	/* PCIe only */
+	{ 0x00DB, 0x0004 },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x0084, 0x0104 },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x00C4, 0x0104 },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x0085, 0x0005 },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x00C5, 0x0005 },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x0086, 0x0337 },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x00C6, 0x0337 },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x0088, 0x3DBE },	/* COMB0 offset, PCIe value */
+	{ 0x00C8, 0x3DBE },	/* COMB0 offset, PCIe value */
+	{ 0x0082, 0x0003 },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x00C2, 0x0003 },	/* shared with COMB0 */
+	{ 0x009C, 0x0014 },	/* COMB0 offset, PCIe value */
+	{ 0x00DC, 0x0014 },	/* COMB0 offset, PCIe value */
+	{ 0x009E, 0x0192 },	/* COMB0 offset, PCIe value */
+	{ 0x00DE, 0x0192 },	/* COMB0 offset, PCIe value */
+	{ 0x009F, 0x0006 },	/* COMB0 offset, PCIe value */
+	{ 0x00DF, 0x0006 },	/* COMB0 offset, PCIe value */
+	{ 0x81E0, 0x0000 },	/* PCIe only */
+	{ 0x8171, 0x0019 },	/* PCIe only */
+	{ 0x8172, 0x0019 },	/* PCIe only */
+	{ 0x81FF, 0x0001 },	/* COMB0 offset, PCIe value */
+};
+
+/*
+ * Three 32-bit read-modify-writes the vendor does on byte offsets 0x98, 0xa8
+ * and 0xd8 of the PMA window, each clearing [1:0] and setting 0b10.
+ *
+ * ⚠ These are byte offsets on a window every other access treats as 16-bit
+ * words, so one 32-bit access covers two PMA words -- and byte 0x98 is word
+ * index 0x4C, not index 0x98. Reproduced exactly as the vendor issues them,
+ * because that is what the hardware saw in every boot that worked; whether the
+ * intent was the word pair at 0x4C/0x4D or the words at index 0x98 is unsettled.
+ */
+static const u32 a733_pcie_pma_sel_bytes[] = { 0x98, 0xa8, 0xd8 };
+
+static int a733_pcie_phy_init(struct phy *phy)
+{
+	struct a733_pcie_combophy *cp = phy_get_drvdata(phy);
+	u32 val;
+	int ret, i;
+
+	ret = clk_set_rate(cp->serdes_clk, 100000000);
+	if (ret)
+		return dev_err_probe(cp->dev, ret, "serdes clock to 100 MHz\n");
+
+	ret = clk_prepare_enable(cp->serdes_clk);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	ret = clk_prepare_enable(cp->refclk);
+	if (ret)
+		goto err_serdes;
+
+	/* COMB1 carries PCIe, not USB3. Reset value of this field is 0xF. */
+	writel(A733_PCIE_PIPE_TXD_MAP_PCIE0, cp->top2 + A733_PCIE_PIPE_TXD_MAP);
+
+	writel(A733_PCIE_LINK_CTRL1_INIT, cp->link + A733_PCIE_LINK_CTRL1);
+
+	a733_pcie_pma_write_all(cp, a733_pcie_pma_pre,
+				ARRAY_SIZE(a733_pcie_pma_pre));
+
+	/* lane mode 00 = PCIe across the PIPE interface (UM: L00_MODE) */
+	a733_pcie_rmw(cp->link + A733_PCIE_LANE0_CTRL0, A733_PCIE_LANE0_MODE, 0);
+
+	a733_pcie_pma_write_all(cp, a733_pcie_pma_post,
+				ARRAY_SIZE(a733_pcie_pma_post));
+
+	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(a733_pcie_pma_sel_bytes); i++)
+		a733_pcie_rmw(cp->pma + a733_pcie_pma_sel_bytes[i], 0x3, 0x2);
+
+	/* release the PHY, then the lane */
+	a733_pcie_rmw(cp->link + A733_PCIE_LINK_CTRL0, 0, A733_PCIE_LINK_RESET_N);
+	a733_pcie_rmw(cp->link + A733_PCIE_LANE0_CTRL0, 0,
+		      A733_PCIE_LANE0_RESET_N_SW);
+
+	/*
+	 * Wait for the PMA common block. The vendor spins here forever; a PHY
+	 * that never reports ready must fail the probe, not hang the boot. The
+	 * bound is generous on purpose -- the observed time is far below it and
+	 * this is not a place to be clever.
+	 */
+	ret = readl_poll_timeout(cp->link + A733_PCIE_LINK_STUS0, val,
+				 val & A733_PCIE_PMA_CMN_READY, 100, 100000);
+	if (ret) {
+		dev_err(cp->dev, "PMA common block not ready (STUS0 %#x)\n", val);
+		goto err_refclk;
+	}
+
+	/*
+	 * Post-ready fixups, in the vendor's order. The first one is a plain
+	 * constant: the vendor reads the word and computes 0x220 | ~0x2 from it
+	 * before overwriting the result with 0x270 unconditionally, so the read
+	 * and the arithmetic never had an effect and are not reproduced.
+	 */
+	writew(0x0270, cp->pma + 0xa0);
+	writew(readw(cp->pma + 0x98) | BIT(4), cp->pma + 0x98);
+	writew(readw(cp->pma + 0x18000) | BIT(0), cp->pma + 0x18000);
+
+	/* reference clock out to the slot, last, once the PHY is up */
+	a733_pcie_rmw(cp->link + A733_PCIE_LINK_CTRL1, 0,
+		      A733_PCIE_LINK_EN_REFCLK);
+
+	return 0;
+
+err_refclk:
+	clk_disable_unprepare(cp->refclk);
+err_serdes:
+	clk_disable_unprepare(cp->serdes_clk);
+	return ret;
+}
+
+static int a733_pcie_phy_exit(struct phy *phy)
+{
+	struct a733_pcie_combophy *cp = phy_get_drvdata(phy);
+
+	a733_pcie_rmw(cp->link + A733_PCIE_LANE0_CTRL0,
+		      A733_PCIE_LANE0_RESET_N_SW, 0);
+	a733_pcie_rmw(cp->link + A733_PCIE_LINK_CTRL0,
+		      A733_PCIE_LINK_RESET_N, 0);
+	clk_disable_unprepare(cp->refclk);
+	clk_disable_unprepare(cp->serdes_clk);
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static const struct phy_ops a733_pcie_phy_ops = {
+	.init	= a733_pcie_phy_init,
+	.exit	= a733_pcie_phy_exit,
+	.owner	= THIS_MODULE,
+};
+
+static int a733_pcie_combophy_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
+{
+	struct device *dev = &pdev->dev;
+	struct a733_pcie_combophy *cp;
+	struct phy_provider *provider;
+	struct resource *res;
+	int ret;
+
+	cp = devm_kzalloc(dev, sizeof(*cp), GFP_KERNEL);
+	if (!cp)
+		return -ENOMEM;
+
+	cp->dev = dev;
+
+	cp->link = devm_platform_ioremap_resource(pdev, 0);
+	if (IS_ERR(cp->link))
+		return PTR_ERR(cp->link);
+	/*
+	 * devm_ioremap(), not devm_platform_ioremap_resource(): the top-2
+	 * window at 0x06C06000 holds the protocol mux of BOTH combo PHYs, and
+	 * the COMB0 driver already claims it as an exclusive region. Requesting
+	 * it a second time fails with -EBUSY and takes PCIe down whenever USB3
+	 * probed first -- an ordering nobody controls. The AUX/HPD PHY solves
+	 * the same overlap the same way.
+	 */
+	res = platform_get_resource(pdev, IORESOURCE_MEM, 1);
+	if (!res)
+		return -EINVAL;
+	cp->top2 = devm_ioremap(dev, res->start, resource_size(res));
+	if (!cp->top2)
+		return -ENOMEM;
+	cp->pma = devm_platform_ioremap_resource(pdev, 2);
+	if (IS_ERR(cp->pma))
+		return PTR_ERR(cp->pma);
+
+	cp->serdes_clk = devm_clk_get(dev, "serdes");
+	if (IS_ERR(cp->serdes_clk))
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(cp->serdes_clk),
+				     "serdes clock\n");
+
+	cp->refclk = devm_clk_get(dev, "refclk");
+	if (IS_ERR(cp->refclk))
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(cp->refclk), "refclk gate\n");
+
+	/*
+	 * The SERDES reset is shared with the USB3 side of the subsystem, so it
+	 * is taken as a shared reference and deasserted here; devres balances
+	 * it. Asserting it on exit would take the other half down with us.
+	 */
+	cp->reset = devm_reset_control_get_shared(dev, NULL);
+	if (IS_ERR(cp->reset))
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(cp->reset), "serdes reset\n");
+
+	ret = reset_control_deassert(cp->reset);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	cp->phy = devm_phy_create(dev, NULL, &a733_pcie_phy_ops);
+	if (IS_ERR(cp->phy))
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(cp->phy), "phy_create\n");
+
+	phy_set_drvdata(cp->phy, cp);
+
+	provider = devm_of_phy_provider_register(dev, of_phy_simple_xlate);
+
+	return PTR_ERR_OR_ZERO(provider);
+}
+
+static const struct of_device_id a733_pcie_combophy_of_match[] = {
+	{ .compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-pcie-combophy" },
+	{ }
+};
+MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, a733_pcie_combophy_of_match);
+
+static struct platform_driver a733_pcie_combophy_driver = {
+	.probe	= a733_pcie_combophy_probe,
+	.driver	= {
+		.name		= "sun60i-a733-pcie-combophy",
+		.of_match_table	= a733_pcie_combophy_of_match,
+	},
+};
+module_platform_driver(a733_pcie_combophy_driver);
+
+MODULE_DESCRIPTION("Allwinner A733 COMB1 combo-PHY, PCIe personality");
+MODULE_LICENSE("GPL");
